{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires","id":1460237,"title":"[World-building] How bad are your vampires?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-17T11:56:40-07:00","id":1460237,"title":"[World-building] How bad are your vampires?","content":"Every Storyteller has their own preferences for how they like to portray being a monster. &quot;Personal Horror&quot; was the byline of the original game with the idea the player characters would portray a reluctant monster that was horrified by the actions they might undertake under the influence of either the Beast or the Hunger. Some fans HATE Personal Horror. They prefer to play monsters who revel in their vampiric power or hate the idea of feeling guilt over feeding on what nature clearly intended as their food.<br /> <br /> Others have a preference for vampires who are different sort of monster who prey upon the evil doer and are more Nick Knight or Angel than cursed monster.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/forever_knight.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This is mostly about PCs, though, when people typically discuss it. PCs are able to defy the nature of their curse far differently than the majority of vampires. This is more a thread about how bad you think vampires in general are and specific groups ranging from Clans, Camarilla, and so on. How high is the average vamp's Humanity? What does that really mean? How often do they become wights?<br /> <br /> A general all purpose discussion of how dark being one of the undead and their life is morally and ethically.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T12:42:31-07:00","id":1460244,"title":"","content":"How bad are vampires in my campaigns?<br /> <br /> <b>Neontes and Ancilla</b><br /> <br /> I generally try and go with the idea that the majority of vampires after their Fledgling area tend to stabilize their Humanity at around Humanity 5-6. They try not to kill people and feel guilt when it happens but they are people who have ended up killing at least one or two innocents in their life. Its almost inevitable and all of them are carrying the weight of innocent blood. Those Fledglings or Neonates that try to live &quot;cruelty free&quot; lives of animal blood or bagging are generally considered to be pathetic and subject of mockery. There's a lot of peer pressure and reassurance from the culture of Kindred that feeding on humans and the fact they occassionally die is something that is okay. They do exist, though, with 7-8 Humanity but this a stressful isolating life.<br /> <br /> Use of Disciplines on mortals and ghouling humans is considered perfectly normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Elders</b><br /> <br /> Elders tend to have the view of Humanity 3-4 to me with the best ones being around Humanity 5 with rare exceptions. The centuries just wear them down and they become incredibly jaded about killing for the slightest provocation. Elders tend to revel in their power and hedonism with few caring about their fellow vampires let alone humanity. Generally, Elders tend to have the weakness of having alienated their former coteries and friends so they are usually solo except for their progeny and other vampires they enslaved. This helps make them vulnerable to groups of younger vampires working together.<br /> <br /> In ages prior, almost all Elders became on a Road rather than Humanity but the lack of those in the Modern Era has caused a decent chunk to fall to the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Wights</b><br /> <br /> Only a handful of vampires manage to live to be Elders. A decent chunk of newly Embraced vampires simply never get control over their Beasts and rapidly degenerate to wightdom in their first year. They kill, love it, and continue until they become a monster. This is the origin of why releasing a childe from his sire's control is a Tradition. Those vampires who degenerate after their &quot;release&quot; time generally come in two varieties. The first are <b>Diablerists</b> who are forever cursed thereafter with a lust for cannibalism. Even once can be enough to send you on a spiral down to the Beast. The second are those who have lost all of their immediate loved ones or associates in some catastrophic event. Elders are especially prone to this.<br /> <br /> <b>Anarchs vs. Camarilla</b><br /> <br /> The Camarilla is better than the Sabbat in that it doesn't actively disdain and hate humanity but the irony of the Anarchs are they tend to be either better or worse than the Camarilla. There are Anarchs who believe they should be better than the Ivory Tower and those who utterly revel in their Beasts like miniature Sabbat. Camarilla vampires tend to be far more consistent.<br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat</b><br /> <br /> I go full grindhouse horror movies with a dose of Cthulhu for Sabbat. The majority of Sabbat are Humanity 1-3 with them having far more examples of those going Wight. However, if you manage to reach Ancilla-dom (at least 50 years) then you might be accepted to study one of the Paths of Enlightenment that usually require a decade of study to really master.<br /> <br /> Ironically, in my games, only a handful of Sabbat ever get higher than 5-6 in a Path because the Sabbat's demands detract from truly immersing yourself in one's spiritual mysteries.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-17-2021, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T12:47:20-07:00","id":1460246,"title":"","content":"Like a lot of things, this has varied across editions and it can be helpful shorthand for GMs to say what edition's take they prefer.<br /> <br /> <b>In 1e</b>, you had assholes like Son and Jacob Schumpter and Gordon Keaton. But you had may more &quot;good guy&quot; vampires too. Johann, Maldavis, Rebekah, etc., there was a pretty decent number of Humanity 8+ vampires. Probably at least as many as the Humanity 0 ones (back when Humanity 0 didn't equate to wightdom). Golconda was something a decent number of vampires could tangibly achieve. The Inconnu were a brotherhood of good guys.<br /> <br /> Basically, vampires could be saints or monsters or anything in between. Any given city is likely to have vampires from all those groups.<br /> <br /> <b>2e</b> dialed back on the number of good guys in the setting. Lots of the saintly type vampires in Chicago got killed off in the book's 2e update. <i>D.C. by Night </i>gave us monsters like Marcus Vitel and relatively decent vampires like Amos, who wasn't pursuing Golconda but also seemed like a decent and compassionate enough dude. The Inconnu were still portrayed as a benign force but occupied the spotlight less. Saulot was Vampire Jesus. Lucita was the rebellious eternal Anarch against her sire.<br /> <br /> Basically, vampires could decent people or monsters or anything in between. Saints are rare enough that your city might not have any.<br /> <br /> <b>Revised</b> cast everything in a darker and more sinister light. Pretty much everyone was an asshole. Not literally true, I can think of some decent vampires from Revised, but the setting as a whole grew much grimmer. Pogroms against the thin-bloods and sectarian wars against the Sabbat became the order of the day. The Inconnu were cast as much a much more mysterious force that could be benign or sinister depending on the GM's preference. Depending on the book you're reading, Saulot was either a monster as evil and manipulative as any other Antediluvian (<i>Clanbook Salubri</i>) or a rare light in a world of darkness (<i>Lair of the Hidden</i>). Lucita murders a bunch of orphans to join the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Basically, vampires are mostly jerks, monsters are common, and saints are so rare it's up to the GM whether or not they exist.<br /> <br /> <b>V20</b> is a lot like 2e and adopts a more balanced take. One of my favorite characters was a cleaver parent who's protective of her young son and is mentioned as being pretty ruthless in her hunting methods, but cares about his welfare over all else. She hasn't turned him into a ghoul or let him know she's a vampire. Also, the Inconnu are a mystery. They might be benign or sinister or something in between, depending on the GM.<br /> <br /> <b>V5 </b>basically hits you over the head with a tire iron that has &quot;VAMPIRES ARE MONSTERS&quot; written over the sides. Pet play enthusiasts murder their dommes and giggle about it. Vampire cleavers don't only turn kids into ghouls, they turn babies into them too, and kill nosy social workers for being nosy and complain about what a hassle it is. Anarchs giggle that diablerie feels good and you deserve to feel good. The darkness and assholery gets so omnipresent that the writers start to play it for comedy, because the books would be too bleak if they didn't.<br /> <br /> Basically, vampires are monsters, and you're kidding yourself if you believe otherwise.<br /> <br /> <br /> I prefer the V20 take. Vampires are predators, and it can be an easy slide from that towards monstrosity, but some vampires still manage to be okay people. Some humans manage to be worse monsters than vampires. I don't think the realities of vampiric predation or the Camarilla's cutthroat politics should be discounted, but neither do I think it makes for an interesting setting just to make all vampires assholes. You need light to contrast the darkness and give real tragedy to the vampires who let darkness overtake them. Because there <i>is</i> another way. It's just harder.<br /> <br /> In my experience, PCs usually don't defy the nature of their curse. They tend to become more monstrous over the course of the chronicle. Being a monster is more expedient and offers more paths to power. That's why a lot of vampires eventually succumb, and why the answer to &quot;How high is the average vamp's Humanity?&quot; varies by age. Your average neonate is still the person they were alive, albeit more jaded, but the older you get the more monstrous you're likely to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T12:53:23-07:00","id":1460248,"title":"","content":"As a related aside, &quot;virgin&quot; is a slang term in my setting for vampires who've never killed a human being.<br /> <br /> Like in the real world, the Camarilla views individuals who boast about it as sanctimonious and possibly lying.<br /> <br /> Virgin neonates exist, but Kindred tend to view virgin ancillae and elders as urban legends. No one ever seems to personally know one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T17:43:51-07:00","id":1460270,"title":"","content":"My vampires are generally sufficiently evil that I don\u2019t bother with the Humanity system for them. Most Camarilla vampires, outside of neonates, will anyone that they need to if it is practical to do so, including innocents and/or children and they won\u2019t feel much if any remorse for doing so. The Sabbat are the Sabbat and they will kill innocents even when it may be unwise to do so. The Anarchs are disproportionately young and still have some vampires who are a bit squeamish about hurting people, but the leaders of the movement are just as cold blooded, maybe even crueler, than Camarilla elders.<br /> <br /> That isn\u2019t to say that good vampires are impossible, I still have some NPCs who are actually moral and humane, maybe even with high humanity or aspirations for Golconda, so they are the exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T17:58:29-07:00","id":1460272,"title":"","content":"Vampirism brings out the worst tendencies of people, but it takes time before the Beast erodes Humanity. So most brand new neonates will average around Humanity 6-7. Let's called it 6.5. Most elders will be at Humanity 4-5, or 4.5. Ancilla are therefore likely around 5.5. Probably 80% of vampires in those categories will easily fit within that range. <br /> <br /> But a significant number (20%) will have lower Humanity. Those will include the real sociopaths and monsters. And will include those in power who have needed to kill to either maintain the vampire social order or to defend their own hold on power. Humanity 3 could be the default of many hardened Princes or elders, but if they indulge their dark side (as opposed to doing the brutality that is necessary and then stopping), they won't last long. But I don't discount the possibility that some of the vampires who hold office may have unsuspected high levels of Conscience, but are able to hide that aspect of them to avoid the appearance of weakness but that enables them to hold more Humanity than they &quot;should&quot; be having.<br /> <br /> I think any vampire who gets to Humanity 2 won't be around too long. By that point, it's too easy to lose what you have because the vampire is so inured to evil that they may think they've fallen as far as they can and won't recognize the steps that bring them to 1 or 0. The only reason I don't we see many Wights in the setting is that once a vampire is seen as being at this level, the elders make sure he is put down like a dog before he descends into being a Wight. Although another possibility is any such Wights, aided by their Disciplines, manage to effectively disappear and prey on others in secret, like Gollum searching for the One Ring keeping out of sight.<br /> <br /> Humane, high humanity vampires will always be an outlier. I think most vampires will have any high Humanity tendencies beaten out of then while they are fledglings. This will either be a result of their sire &quot;helping&quot; them with their condition so they accept that &quot;accidents will happen,&quot; or that they demonstrate they are unable to hack it and therefore are destroyed before they ever get released. Those that manage to get through the system and be the Nick Knights or Hannibal Kings quickly decide they have to avoid other vampires as much as possible for the same reason recovering drug addicts should stay away from other drug addicts. They'll just slide into the bad behavior. So they isolate themselves from other vampires and try to avoid situations that will arouse the Beast. In this case, I think a character like Hannibal King (a neonate who as a repeating background character in comics doesn't deal in much action despite being a private detective) is more likely to succeed than Nick Knight (an elder who actively fights violent crime in an exciting TV series who routinely deals with other vampires). But such &quot;natural&quot; high Humanity vampires do exist, just not in every domain. And those that do will be alone, few in number, and probably virtually unknown to other vampires.<br /> <br /> There's another category of high Humanity vampires, and it are those older vampires who have noticed that their Humanity has fallen drastically and are entering panic mode. They desperately want to something about it. It is these vampires that become involved in the various schemes to understand Golconda, contact the Children of Osiris, or more crackpot schemes to recover Humanity. Since most of these vampires do so out of self-serving nature, they are doomed to fail. But a minority of them actually have their conscience rewoke and can make sincere, though likely temporary, progress at restoring Humanity.<br /> <br /> If you view the Inconnu being a sect really concerned about high Humanity vampires and Golconda seekers, then they exist to &quot;collect&quot; the truly outstanding vampires and try to protect and guide them. But such things can only happen if they take said vampires away from vampire society (taking a PC out of the game).<br /> <br /> I imagine most vampires in the Camarilla probably have prolonged periods when things are stable and they can keep their Humanity high. However, prolonged praxis struggles and sect conflicts force them into prolonged periods of violence where their Humanity plunges. But since many of those vampires are destroyed during that time, they get replaced by recently made vampires of High Humanity. The surviving ones in turn are &quot;promoted&quot; within their society becoming the next generation of leaders or ancillae, or surviving until they become elders.<br /> <br /> PCs in my experience start out at levels 6 or 7, and have a steady decline to level 4 or 5. I've seen a few PCs work hard to remain at level 7, but most give up sometime during the chronicle. I've only had 1 PC who was truly interested in playing a humane vampire, and in effect she was more like an NPC doing her own scenes with ties to the PC coterie rather than a member of the coterie itself. I think she started at 7 and managed to convince me that Humanity 8 was achieved. I gave it to her just to encourage her.<br /> <br /> I don't play Sabbat, but as the generic vampires are monsters set, they clearly have a lot less Humanity. CTPHipps' description of them seems to fit what I'd do with them too.<br /> <br /> I think vampires are soulless monsters that should be destroyed whenever encountered. But that doesn't mean some can't hold onto their humanity. They might never truly be &quot;good&quot;, but they can definitely choose not to do evil and that counts for something. &quot;Good&quot; vampires need to be destroyed as well, but they have a chance of redeeming their souls when that happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T18:09:00-07:00","id":1460277,"title":"","content":"I tend to reject the idea of the &quot;degeneration after a certain point becomes faster.&quot; Basically, when you reach Humanity 1-2, you are certainly only a step away from losing yourself to wassail but to lose that lingering bit of humanity requires something truly horrifyingly evil. Either diablerie or something utterly repulsive like a Toreador Antitribu party or mass murder of the innocent in a particularly sadistic way.<br /> <br /> Vampires also do have a little bit of &quot;bounce&quot; rather than a straight shot from 10 to 0 in one direction. At least vampires in the Camarilla and Anarchs often have moments where they become invested in some human and tries to do something good for them. There's plenty of vampire stalking or attempts to make themselves feel better about something. This is just a stop gap measure and eventually they will lose but they try to feel &quot;alive&quot; and sometimes it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T19:09:13-07:00","id":1460286,"title":"","content":"The mechanics (I\u2019m not fully familiar with V5 yet, but previous ones) certainly don\u2019t support the idea that vampire with a low Humanity don\u2019t last long. Those low Humanity values of 1-3 could last a vampire for millennia without ever becoming a wight. I mean, at 2 you can murder someone, not feel guilty about it, and be just fine - unless you turn into Ramsey Bolton, you probably won\u2019t drop below 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> That makes sense to me, because that is how I see the majority of vampires - willing to murder if it benefits them but don\u2019t make a point of pointlessly killing or inflicting unnecessary suffering. So about 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T19:16:11-07:00","id":1460289,"title":"","content":"I avoid the edgelord shit, run the whole panoply of potential outlooks and path ratings, and try to portray vampires as ideologically and ethically diverse as possible...within the constraints of them all being immortal bloodsuckers with Jekyll-and-Hyde syndromes. The one hard rule I mind, is that PC's <i>aren't</i> any different than NPC's, and I make sure the NPC's I introduce and run regularly are as complex, nuanced, and proactive as any PC within reasonable expectation. And, I work <i>very</i> hard to subvert and twist those expectations.<br /> <br /> One example from my current TC game, is during one of the more recent downtimes, Sherazina died of old age. Sherazina being the revenant NPC the PC's run into during the first published story, who is Dragomir Basarab's biological sister. Without going into details, she ended up in the dubious stewardship of none other than <i>Vykos</i>. With Vykos as her domitor, one would have expected her to have an unspeakably painful and short life before being dumped, forgotten before she'd even died, in an unmarked, shallow, grave.<br /> <br /> Nope.<br /> <br /> He gifted her to Dragomir in her sunset years, so she could return home and die in peace surrounded by loved ones, after a lifetime of dutiful, if not always pleasant, service. Just the tiniest, most seemingly insignificant, act of humanity in a time of great strife and suffering, and from the <i>last</i> vampire one would expect.<br /> <br /> I wanted to remind my players that, whatever...<i>thing...</i>Vykos is now, <i>isn't</i> what Vykos always was. It <i>used to be</i> a proud and noble Cainite with a deeply philosophical bent named Myca, who appeared to the PC's in an hour of need and gave them a helping hand to perform a vital task to secure their shared future. Or, perhaps more accurately...whatever Vykos is <i>now</i>, despite all of the horrific and despicable shit it's done least of all to the PC's, it holds within it <i>some</i> lingering shred of humanity that would drive it to perform an act of unwarranted and gratuitous kindness.<br /> <br /> Outside the realm of PC, or player, knowledge...was it Vykos or the Dracon who made the decision to send Sherazina home to die? Was it a moment of clarity for the ill-fated Myca, or was it a moment of vicarious pleasure for the methuselah whose only, denied, wish was to die? Does it matter?<br /> <br /> Sometimes, the most monstrous thing you can do in a chronicle, is the <i>least</i> monstrous thing. It keeps the players guessing, and uncertainty is the greatest personal horror of all. In this particular case, the question of the hour was, &quot;are we more monstrous than <i>Vykos</i>?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-17-2021, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T21:13:03-07:00","id":1460297,"title":"","content":"Bad and vile, but mostly in banal and tedious ways rather than in theatrical ways. They are the personification of Hannah Arendt's idea of the banality of evil, the occasional Sabbat theatrics aside. They are just vanity and self indulgence. There is nothing worth redeeming in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T09:15:14-07:00","id":1460339,"title":"","content":"First of all I find Grimdark incredibly boring. It is just as boring to me in Vampire as it is in Warhammer 40k. It also hardly keeps my suspension of disbelief for long, as absolute evil is simply stupid.<br /> <br /> But on top of that I find that shadowing human cruelty with or depicting a &quot;race&quot; as inherently evil is of bad taste. A vampire is a normal person trapped in a fantastical circumstance, but still a person.<br /> <br /> So I tend to give them a wide berth, they are varied. Most of them will get more cynical with age, but cynicism isn't the same as low or high Humanity. Many people with rose-tinted glasses are perfectly capable of monstrous cruelty just to make the world conform to their views, while many a cynical just gets better at resisting the social pressure and hold to their beliefs and conscious without expecting the world to respond accordingly. I see this all the time in the bank I work at.<br /> <br /> People in places of power sometimes are worse, but that is not a rule. The callousness we perceive on them frequently comes more from POV, lack of information on both sides, and several other elements than they being really evil persons. <b>Systems</b> are colder than the people that form them, and can be more or less evil than them even at the top.<br /> <br /> With all that in mind I don't even buy that elders are necessarily significantly less Humane than neonates. Certainly there is a difference, as both extremes tend to be weeded out by natural selection, but even that is because extremes <i>tend</i> to be born of unadaptive behaviors, and not because they're unadaptive on their own. As it is, elders in high positions also tend to be a little lower, but not by much, specially because they're exposed to an even greater adaptive pressure.<br /> <br /> This is especially true if you consider the effects of Humanity at each level. The lower you are, the less likely you are to even care about things. What is social power to a Humanity 2 vampire? Why a vampire at this level would even bother to be Prince? Good or evil, politics is an extremely person-involved endeavor. It is also time consuming and requires resources as much as it generates. It requires ambitions, be them selfish or generous, far beyond personal survival. A Humanity 1-2 vampire is more likely to appreciate being jobless and left alone. So there is as much or a greater pressure for being high Humanity in politics as there is for being low.<br /> <br /> I never thought Evil\u2122 made for interesting characters, not even villains, and I'm more interested in playing how the system and the feeding pressure vampires to either adapt or fall, with adapting including finding your personal Humanity niche at any level, than playing vampires being a race of greater jerks than humans already are.<br /> <br /> None of this affects PCs, though. PCs are what their players want to be, and most will fall from grace simply because they're finding the accommodating spot for what they want out of the game. Since RPG is also a form of escapism, it makes sense for most players to want to do things they can't even consider in real life, like killing. They're not typical characters, they're player avatars and vessels for the player's needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T11:31:20-07:00","id":1460352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460339#post1460339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on top of that I find that shadowing human cruelty with or depicting a &quot;race&quot; as inherently evil is of bad taste. A vampire is a normal person trapped in a fantastical circumstance, but still a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is supposed to be the nature of the vampire &quot;curse&quot; that you are a normal person who is cursed to do horrifying evil by the Beast and Hunger against your will.<br /> <br /> But you don't want to die.<br /> <br /> So your choices are:<br /> <br /> 1. Become evil to stop feeling terrible all the time.<br /> <br /> 2. Feel terrible all the time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T11:43:45-07:00","id":1460354,"title":"","content":"Meh. I think this is an extremely boring simplification of both the circumstances and the human nature. So no, the idea of vampire = evil is something I neither buy or find interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T14:40:50-07:00","id":1460369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460354#post1460354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. I think this is an extremely boring simplification of both the circumstances and the human nature. So no, the idea of vampire = evil is something I neither buy or find interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends whether someone means individual vampires or all vampires.<br /> <br /> As far as <b>individual vampires</b> go, I enjoy my share of vampires who are doing their best to maintain their humanity. Some of them even manage to turn their existences into a (net) positive good by keeping the worst excesses of their fellow undead in check. The True Brujah narrator in <i>Sins of the Blood</i> spends his unlife hunting wights and pursuing Golconda. (He also failed to obtain it and committed suicide afterwards, which was a fun spin on the &quot;saintly Golcondite&quot; archetype.) If you have one high Humanity vampire who kills X people over their unlife, but who destroys another vampire that would kill 10 times that number of people, then you could make the argument that vampire #1's existence was a (net) positive good. You can have middling-Humanity princes whose reigns cause less death and suffering than lower Humanity elders hungry to seize the throne. Vampire hunters who take out that prince might indirectly cause the deaths of more people than they save. Even a Humanity 3 tyrant prince might be a positive good if they're the only thing keeping the Sabbat from taking over the city. The potential for good and evil exists in all Kindred at all levels of Humanity, and even &quot;evil&quot; Kindred can still lead existences that are a (net) positive good for humanity.<br /> <br /> This is also the primary reason I don't accept the &quot;any vampire who doesn't kill themselves is a bad person&quot; argument a gamer I know once made. If you're a vampire and your main goal in unlife is &quot;just keep existing&quot;, or &quot;accumulate power and influence&quot;, then I think it's a pretty reasonable argument that you're making an ignorant choice at best and a grossly selfish choice at worst. You are going to kill people, probably multiple people, possibly many people. But if you seek to mitigate the harm caused by your fellow undead, or to protect and provide for your mortal family, or any number of other altruistic intentions, well, I think you might have a valid argument that not killing yourself isn't a selfish choice. <i>Might</i>. You could still become a monster anyway despite your good intentions. Road to hell is paved with those.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to <b>all</b> <b>vampires</b>? Almost all vampires eventually become murderers, and repeat murderers at that. Google's first search result tells me &quot;1 in 1,167&quot; is a liberal estimate for the number of humans in the world who kill another human. Less than 1%. The number of vampires who kill someone at some point in their unlives is probably over 99%. That's a pretty staggering figure to consider, and I think you can pretty easily argue that the majority of those killings aren't morally justified.<br /> <br /> So, if I lived in the WoD and could press a button to make every vampire on earth spontaneously combust, that wouldn't be a hard choice. You'd save unthinkably many lives, all before considering the various other forms of harm vampires cause. A lot gets made about vampirism being a curse, but it's a curse upon humanity as much as the Kindred themselves. Vampires are (an) evil.<br /> <br /> The nuanced and interesting parts of the setting, for me, are how characters respond to evil, rather than debating whether evil exists. One of the lowest Humanity PCs in my current game (essentially) accepted the Embrace to save her mother from an abusive scumbag husband. Her intentions were good and her actions achieved real and lasting good. Was the PC becoming a monster inevitable? Could she have made other choices? If not, was saving her mother worth it? Can you accomplish good ends through evil means? These aren't questions with easy answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T14:56:12-07:00","id":1460370,"title":"","content":"I tend to hover towards vampires having rules and hangups of varying scales, l can't really be bothered running humanity for all NPC's unless it's a plot point but I tend to hint at rules,redeeming traits and limits to what they do. For example the Tremere regent in an old game never harmed children and was very supportive of subordinates I also recall as Lasombra who was personally affable on a day to day basis and was protective of her human friends....although she did systematically embrace them all over 2 decades so her moral core was a little of kilter even if her reasons were quite sympathetic. Both these characters where cold blooded killers but the added layers hinted at how they're staving off the beast. Playing a complete sociopath is going to annoy the players when they're unable to engage in simular antics plus personally hating all the npcs gets demoralizing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T16:35:47-07:00","id":1460387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460369#post1460369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends whether someone means individual vampires or all vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no, I totally dig your argument. Vampires as a thing existing is an evil upon the world, surely.<br /> <br /> What I was talking was indeed the approach that just being a vampire turns someone into an evil person. Not an existence that is harming to the world due its natural necessities, but someone who is Evil as a person. That is the concept I find boring, precisely because it eliminates the examination upon the themes.<br /> <br /> Its the one D&amp;D thing that I dislike, and that a lot of players apply in WoD: Vampire means Chaotic Evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T16:44:03-07:00","id":1460388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460387#post1460387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, no, I totally dig your argument. Vampires as a thing existing is an evil upon the world, surely.<br /> <br /> What I was talking was indeed the approach that just being a vampire turns someone into an evil person. Not an existence that is harming to the world due its natural necessities, but someone who is Evil as a person. That is the concept I find boring, precisely because it eliminates the examination upon the themes.<br /> <br /> Its the one D&amp;D thing that I dislike, and that a lot of players apply in WoD: Vampire means Chaotic Evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the distinction is actually as fine cut as you might think. I mean in D&amp;D and movies, you have people turned into vampires and they automatically are evil and want to kill their loved ones. That's silly unless they're possessed by demons ala Buffy. However, in V:TM, you might justifiably argue anyone who makes the selfish choice to continue existing as a vampire to be at least a little morally compromised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T17:01:43-07:00","id":1460390,"title":"","content":"The very idea that a person as a whole is morally compromised is an absurd simplification of the question that doesn't interest me. Pointing that the process isn't instantaneous or clear cut (and it isn't in D&amp;D and movies, either, unless when a specif author wants to) doesn't change that it's simplistic and that I find it uninteresting in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T17:08:48-07:00","id":1460392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460390#post1460390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very idea that a person as a whole is morally compromised is an absurd simplification of the question that doesn't interest me. Pointing that the process isn't instantaneous or clear cut (and it isn't in D&amp;D and movies, either, unless when a specif author wants to) doesn't change that it's simplistic and that I find it uninteresting in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet you are biologically driven to kill and murder rages. How is it not morally compromised by the curse?<br /> <br /> How do you handle these things in-game if you are not cursed? Please explain.<br /> <br /> I'm very curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T17:13:51-07:00","id":1460394,"title":"","content":"I've said what I had to about this in my first post. I'm not talking about how I apply the rules (I use RAW, generally). I'm talking about how bad are my vampires (as stated in the thread's title). You don't need other rules to have a different interpretation on how such a world would look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T17:30:46-07:00","id":1460396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460394#post1460394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said what I had to about this in my first post. I'm not talking about how I apply the rules (I use RAW, generally). I'm talking about how bad are my vampires (as stated in the thread's title). You don't need other rules to have a different interpretation on how such a world would look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying how do vampires not become bad in your universe? I'm not contradicting you, I'm asking from a place of curiosity. Your preference is noted and I'm intrigued.<br /> <br /> I think you have a very interesting take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T17:37:42-07:00","id":1460399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460388#post1460388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure the distinction is actually as fine cut as you might think. I mean in D&amp;D and movies, you have people turned into vampires and they automatically are evil and want to kill their loved ones. That's silly unless they're possessed by demons ala Buffy. However, in V:TM, you might justifiably argue anyone who makes the selfish choice to continue existing as a vampire to be at least a little morally compromised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think even in those examples you see some nuance. Vampires are evil by default in D&amp;D, but an evil alignment doesn't necessarily equate to &quot;possessed by a demon&quot;. Van Richten's son gets turned into a vampire, and by the rules has an evil alignment, but retains enough of his human self to recognize he has become a monster and to allow his father to kill him. This was in Ravenloft, which takes the firmest &quot;vampires are evil&quot; stance out of any D&amp;D setting.<br /> <br /> I used to think it was stupid how D&amp;D required all of its vampires to be evil, but in hindsight I think I was viewing alignment as more of a straitjacket than it needed to to be. One of my old GMs had a campaign where chromatic (evil) and metallic (gold) dragons worked together at the urgings of Bahamut and Tiamat (their respective good and evil deities) because dragonkind was threatened and the deities cared more about its survival than being &quot;fully faithful&quot; to their alignments. Gary Gygax liked to say two lawful good nations could go to war with one another. One of my favorite fan-made modules for Neverwinter Nights has a chaotic evil character who rapes the protagonist, but can eventually be made to feel regret for his actions and apologize for them. His larger alignment doesn't change, though. He's sorry he hurt the protagonist but remains an asshole to most everyone else. One of the other exceptions being his true neutral boss who he shows unwavering loyalty towards. All of this behavior is within the bounds of something an evil-aligned vampire could do. At least in a game I'd run, anyway.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D requiring its vampires to be evil-aligned was fairly reflective of how most vampires in &quot;serious&quot; vampire stories are. Most vampires in the WoD, if you were to give them D&amp;D alignments, would probably be evil. There'd be some neutrals and a very small number of goods (depending on which edition you're using). The &quot;always X alignment&quot; entry in the Monster Manual isn't meant to cover the &quot;once or twice in a campaign&quot; exceptions like Angel and Spike. Planescape had the idea of risen fiends (demons and devils who've turned to good), so if literal embodiments of their alignments can turn against those, I always figured an exceptional enough vampire could do so too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T18:32:28-07:00","id":1460400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460396#post1460396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm saying how do vampires not become bad in your universe? I'm not contradicting you, I'm asking from a place of curiosity. Your preference is noted and I'm intrigued.<br /> <br /> I think you have a very interesting take.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to make it brief and direct for ease of discussion, it's kind of a big question.<br /> <br /> 1 - Lower Humanity reduces your threshold for &quot;sins&quot;, do not force you to commit them. A vampire may stick to a code of conduct higher than its current Humanity rating, so slipping in the code doesn't mean slipping in their actual Humanity;<br /> <br /> 2 - Redemption is a thing. It doesn't have to mean from 3 to 8. If you're plain 7 most of the time, but falls to 6 once in a while (like a decade), you can strive to stay behaving at 7, maybe even 8, and pay the experience for 7. Your behavior pretty much demonstrates that the &quot;sin&quot; is the outlier, but you're stable;<br /> <br /> 3 - No society really works through constant backstabbing and power struggles, esp. a society where becoming a secretary to the Prince in 50 years is considered a meteoric ascension. Most of the time, most of the Kindred are just going through routine and trying to enjoy themselves;<br /> <br /> 4 - By the same token, people in positions of power have to deal with dull administration most of the time and effectiveness and precision are more important in their nightly activities. Although it doesn't means being nice, it pays off more often than not;<br /> <br /> 5 - Doing terrible stuff for the lolz is usually a dumb idea in the long run, and while mortals frequently can escape consequences in the long run, Kindred not so much. Of course, they're still frequently bored and petty, but those two things kind of even themselves out;<br /> <br /> 6 - Vampires are simply still people. Some believe everyone secretly hates everyone else. Some cry watching Titanic. Some will do terrible things and become inured to them. Some will be horrified even more if they notice they're not feeling so bad as they think they should and will look for help;<br /> <br /> 7 - Age doesn't have to work the way we usually depict it as working for immortals, and I think it wouldn't. After some time mortals lose meaning? I've had several dogs and cats through my life, lost them, and my current pets are still like sons to me. Most of the time we ride the moment and barely remember how our life was 10 years ago, we lose loved ones and make new, why would it be different for immortals?<br /> <br /> Not to say that any of this works for everyone, but that those are some of the things that effectively hold vampires from simply becoming a generic bunch of assholes. It is a tough life, full of horror and death, but it isn't really any tougher for nice people than normal life already is, just harder to learn how to cope. Are vampires more skewed towards being assholes? Probably, but not by that much.<br /> <br /> For the opinion that the moral thing to do is to end one's unlife: first off, with which authority can you say that killing yourself is your right? This isn't a clear cut moral question for everyone. But above that, one thing is to say that suicide would be the right thing, but would you do it? Forget about the game, it is one of the most terrible decisions someone makes. Nothing is easy about taking your own life, it goes against every impulse we have and is an extremely desperate decision, eviscerating and terrible. Stop reading pseudo-philosophical crap about suicide and go read scientific papers on the matter and you'll see a world of horror, where no option is an easy option. This &quot;option&quot; shouldn't ever be on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T18:53:51-07:00","id":1460401,"title":"","content":"Thanks! That was an excellent explanation and fascinating set of reasons!<br /> <br /> Much obliged!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T08:09:32-07:00","id":1460432,"title":"","content":"I think it's also important to note the kind of major blowouts that involve multiple vampires committing sins in a rapid basis, only happen once every few decades at most. Shit may go down during a rivalry that heats up, during sieges or large power plays, but nightly unlife tends to be painfully dull. Being kind of an asshole to each other because you're stuck in a Sartrean waking nightmare, isn't a sin unless a vampire is ridiculously high on the minority of paths (Humanity included) that hold consideration of others and charitable behavior as a key precept.<br /> <br /> There's a wide gulf between Elysium snark and having your pawns fuck with another vampire's pawns and domain, which is the worst most vampires do on a nightly basis, and ordering your pawns to engage in open street warfare with another's, attacking another vampire directly, or joining the fray yourself.<br /> <br /> Also, do bear in mind that despite them being a minority, some paths <i>do</i> hold tenets that represent a higher behavioral and ethical standard than Humanity in many ways. Entelechy, Self-Focus, and Redemption come to mind; arguably, Honorable Accord, though how Honorable Accord fits into a potential spectrum of good versus evil depends heavily upon how the vampire interprets the tenets of that path for themselves. Alien they may be, they still defy simple classification along that spectrum.<br /> <br /> And for most of those paths, bear in mind the distinction between committing a sin and actually degenerating. A failed Conscience check represents the slippery slope of accepting and rationalizing the action; a failed Conviction check represents the inability to reconcile the sin with the path being walked and move forward. Most sins <i>don't</i> result in degeneration (at least in mechanical terms, with a reasonable virtue rating), indicating to some degree most vampires don't gleefully degenerate into complete depravity over the course of years or decades, and during the quieter times they seek contrition, or retreat into quiet contemplation, to overcome past transgressions to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T10:21:05-07:00","id":1460439,"title":"","content":"In my mind the vampires that survive, and maybe even succeed, were likely bad people when they were alive. Better people, more moral and ethical people, will probably be the vampires that destroy themselves or are destroyed by hunters or other vampires. But people who are either actively horrible or just inclined that way will adapt most easily - by becoming articulate monsters who ape at the humane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T11:29:34-07:00","id":1460442,"title":"","content":"A person\u2019s biology, circumstances, and opportunities certain can largely determine their moral trajectory. Probably a lot of people who committed terrible acts, like massacres, taking innocent people to death camps or gulags, would have lived relatively moral peaceful lives if they weren\u2019t being given orders to do those bad things.<br /> <br /> Imagine for a moment a married man in a monogamous marriage. Cheating on his wife would be a betrayal of her, so an immoral act. Imagine the following scenarios:<br /> A: a beautiful woman flirts with the married man. He is extremely attracted to her and flirts back, leading to an affair.<br /> B: a woman who isn\u2019t that attractive flirts with the man. He isn\u2019t attracted to her and doesn\u2019t flirt back. There is no affair.<br /> C. The married man had previously developed some health problem which lowers his testosterone and sex drive. The beautiful woman flirts with him and while he thinks she\u2019s pretty, he doesn\u2019t feel that strong desire and doesn\u2019t flirt back, so no affair.<br /> D. The married man is less handsome than in scenario A, the beautiful woman passes by without flirting with him, so there is no affair.<br /> <br /> So we see that this man\u2019s biology and his circumstances can determine whether or not he commits the immoral action.<br /> <br /> Becoming a vampire puts someone into scenario A in so many ways. They now have an incredibly powerful drive to commit potentially harmful acts that they never had before. Furthermore, they have far greater opportunities to commit evil acts - imagine suddenly getting the power to control other people\u2019s minds, to make them your slave. That power would turn many people who think of themselves as nice into slave masters and rapists, which is basically what having a blood bound herd is. Then you\u2019re surrounded by other vampires who are ruthless and will be expecting (or forcing) you to commit certain terrible acts.<br /> <br /> So, a vampire doesn\u2019t have to be evil, they can be more moral than the average human, but most vampires are going to be evil. They are going to commit the occasional murder. They are going to commit acts that are very close to slavery and rape. They probably have a Humanity of 2.<br /> <br /> A 2 Humanity isn\u2019t a murder hobo. Michael Corleone at the end of The Godfather probably had a Humanity of 2. A lot of mobsters, dictators, gang members, or even politicians might have a 2 Humanity. A lot of Game of Thrones characters have a 2 Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T12:06:41-07:00","id":1460447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460442#post1460442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we see that this man\u2019s biology and his circumstances can determine whether or not he commits the immoral action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but this was a terrible example. This example just reinforce the notion that the person isn't at fault for their decisions, and on one of the most common and despicable situations that happen IRL. The notion of a man being a slave to testosterone isn't just scientifically wrong, it has an ugly history.<br /> <br /> I disagree firmly with this take but it is a valid take on vampirsm and my opinion is already posted, but this part is way more offensive than you think it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T13:20:25-07:00","id":1460459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460447#post1460447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but this was a terrible example. This example just reinforce the notion that the person isn't at fault for their decisions, and on one of the most common and despicable situations that happen IRL. The notion of a man being a slave to testosterone isn't just scientifically wrong, it has an ugly history.<br /> <br /> I disagree firmly with this take but it is a valid take on vampirsm and my opinion is already posted, but this part is way more offensive than you think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not a terrible example, it ties the vampiric condition to our real world biological compulsions, which are more subtle but still similar. People aren\u2019t slaves to our hormones, we are still responsible for our decisions, and yet we still suffer from compulsions and desires that are beyond our ability to control.<br /> <br /> For an alcoholic, being offered a drink may cause an overwhelming temptation that requires massive amounts of willpower to resist, for others they don\u2019t even want a drink and it\u2019s no temptation at all. That isn\u2019t a moral difference, the alcoholic genuinely experiences a stronger temptation which is harder to resist. Just as some people experience stronger sexual desires (and related temptations) than other people for complex biological reasons that are usually beyond their control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T15:12:51-07:00","id":1460471,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it an eldar falling to the beast or rising humanity could be an interesting plot point, both could prove disruptive to the power dynamics or even an interesting redemption arc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-19-2021, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T16:47:22-07:00","id":1460480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460459#post1460459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an alcoholic, being offered a drink may cause an overwhelming temptation that requires massive amounts of willpower to resist, for others they don\u2019t even want a drink and it\u2019s no temptation at all. That isn\u2019t a moral difference, the alcoholic genuinely experiences a stronger temptation which is harder to resist. Just as some people experience stronger sexual desires (and related temptations) than other people for complex biological reasons that are usually beyond their control.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great example to draw in parallel to the Beast.<br /> <br /> I rarely drink and have a friend who's an alcoholic. If I have one drink, stopping is easy. If my friend has one drink, stopping is incredibly hard. I wouldn't say either of us is &quot;stronger-willed&quot; than the other. Like you say, alcohol is just a stronger temptation for them than for me.<br /> <br /> As far as alcoholics go, my friend isn't that bad. They don't drink and drive, drink and get physically abusive, or drink while at work. Drinking only really hurts them. But I used to know someone else who would become abusive while they drank and saw no problems with drinking and driving. (They're not in my life anymore.)<br /> <br /> I tend to think of the Beast in a similar way. Any vampire who's exposed to blood is going to be tempted. Any vampire who's exposed to blood while starving is going to be incredibly tempted. There's no way around that. But some vampires are more conscientious about the effects of their addiction than others, some make better decisions about it than others, and some ultimately want to stop being &quot;alcoholics&quot; more than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":".  Typo 09-20-2021, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T18:44:33-07:00","id":1460488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460459#post1460459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not a terrible example</div> </div> </div> </div>The alcoholic is a far better example and one I agree to some extent. Yes, the dynamics of what an urge means to you vary a lot, and the situations aren't equal.<br /> <br /> But a man giving in because a beautiful woman flirted is another kind of situation. It's this part that have an ugly history. A history of unbalanced power in relationships, of women being deemed guilty for the decisions of men, of gaslighting, abuse, rape, financial and emotional violence, with women marked as responsible for how their clothes and moves affect men while those are partially or totally innocent due being poor slaves of their &quot;manliness&quot;.<br /> <br /> And all of that based on an assumption about sexual behavior that was already researched by now and is patently wrong. Those are not the elements that actually affect the likelihood of a man cheating, just the elements used to justify it.<br /> <br /> It is a horrible example steeped in prejudice, abuse and stigmatization of women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T19:16:24-07:00","id":1460491,"title":"","content":"All of that is utterly preposterous. Of course the looks of the woman flirting with a man are going to be a factor in whether or not he cheats with her. Much like offering someone $100 to commit a murder vs $1,000,000 to commit a murder is likely going to affect the likelihood of the hit man agreeing to take a job, it\u2019s still murder (morally and legally) in either case though.<br /> <br /> Though, the point is, whether its sexual behavior or addictive substances, different people have not only different compulsions and strengths of their compulsions but also different opportunities to act on those compulsions. <br /> <br /> Surely, there are many of us who live seemingly virtuous lives but might be committing atrocities if our circumstances changed.<br /> <br /> Becoming a vampire is a really big change of circumstances, not only in that it gives (former) people very strong compulsions that they didn\u2019t previously have, but gives them tremendous power (and thus opportunities) to act on new or old destructive urges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T20:33:17-07:00","id":1460494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460491#post1460491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of that is utterly preposterous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, of course it is. What am I saying, I'm just a female psychologist with specialization in gender studies that tries to keep up with the academic research on the matter. What could I really know about this?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5709195/\" target=\"_blank\">But since I'm also a stubborn woman, let me link to you an article about cheating that starts with a nice revision of the current scientific literature on the matter without a single reference to looks as one of the many factors already proven to affect the likelihood of cheating.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.scielo.br/j/tpsy/a/4b6d4mBhVxNnNmc9bkWcCSw/?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\">Or maybe you prefer to read this article on a comprehensive study on how people experience cheating in their marriages, that identifies the similarities and differences between genders in the experience, but agrees with the larger body of studies in its conclusion that the main drive by far is satisfaction with the current relationship as a source of emotional comfort and sense of security.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.verywellmind.com/why-married-people-cheat-2300656\" target=\"_blank\">If you're not into reading dry scientific articles, you may be more interested in reading an article on a site dedicated to explaining mental health topics to lay people, but with proper revision by psychiatrists?</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.livescience.com/14671-cheating-personality.html\" target=\"_blank\">Short articles from less technical sites like Live Science may interest you better.</a> <a href=\"https://www.bustle.com/p/9-fascinating-things-that-make-people-more-likely-to-cheat-according-to-science-8338602\" target=\"_blank\">Or nice lists from Bustle, although we're starting to thread too far from academy to my taste.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://ifstudies.org/blog/who-cheats-more-the-demographics-of-cheating-in-america\" target=\"_blank\">Maybe the Institute for Family Studies is more your thing, despite their obvious bias in every matter, but they still have some good data.</a><br /> <br /> Note that nowhere you'll find any mention to looks of the person flirting with you nor anything next to it. My personal theory is that it have something to do with a history of studies on the matter systematically finding that this have no bearing at all on the likelihood of cheating. But again, who am I to say that? Maybe they're just bad researchers, all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T21:38:00-07:00","id":1460497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460494#post1460494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, of course it is. What am I saying, I'm just a female psychologist with specialization in gender studies that tries to keep up with the academic research on the matter. What could I really know about this?<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Note that nowhere you'll find any mention to looks of the person flirting with you nor anything next to it. My personal theory is that it have something to do with a history of studies on the matter systematically finding that this have no bearing at all on the likelihood of cheating. But again, who am I to say that? Maybe they're just bad researchers, all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does you being female have to do with anything? Bringing up that, or even your career and education, is just an argument from authority, though a specialization in gender studies may well undermine credibility. Anyway, no need to discuss you here, you did at least link to a bunch of studies.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think any of the things you linked are bad research. Also, none of those studies or articles back up your indignant claims. None of them says that attraction isn\u2019t an issue in cheating nor do they say that testosterone isn\u2019t a factor. <br /> <br /> They second study you link says that attraction is the second most common motive for men to cheat:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201d<span style=\"color:#403D39\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">For the men, &quot;pursuit of freedom, adventure and valorization&quot; was the greatest cause of infidelity, followed by &quot;physical/emotional desire or attraction&quot;.\u201d</span></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#403D39\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <br /> Some of the other articles even say that testosterone levels, as estimated by ring finger length, lead to higher rates of cheating. Another said that sexual excitability lead to higher rates of infidelity.<br /> <br /> There was no evidence provided in any of the studies you spammed me with that attractiveness of the person cheated with isn\u2019t a factor. In fact, it seems like such an odd topic, because of course people who cheat are more likely to do so with people that they are attracted to. Now, one might claim that if someone is the type to cheat, that they will over the course of time find someone who is both willing and attractive. That may well be the statistical trend, but speaking of an individual event, certainly the potential cheater is more likely to cheat with the attractive flirter than the unattractive one. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T21:56:43-07:00","id":1460498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460494#post1460494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, of course it is. What am I saying, I'm just a female psychologist with specialization in gender studies that tries to keep up with the academic research on the matter. What could I really know about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to take these sorts of online claims with a grain of salt. Anyone over a forum can claim to be a psychologist or be using a different definition of &quot;psychologist&quot; than I'm using.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that nowhere you'll find any mention to looks of the person flirting with you nor anything next to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my friends recently expressed, and it's also been my own experience, that most cheating isn't spontaneous. Cheating tends to happen with people who spend time together and establish an emotional connection, vice a spontaneous &quot;I'ma hit that.&quot;<br /> <br /> But when the latter kind of cheating happens, it tends to be with more attractive people. People are more likely to spontaneously cheat on their partners with an attractive alternative (or to get an attractive person to cheat on their partner) than a nonattractive one. We're also more predisposed to want to spend time around attractive people and develop the emotional connections that lead to affairs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460491#post1460491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of that is utterly preposterous. Of course the looks of the woman flirting with a man are going to be a factor in whether or not he cheats with her. Much like offering someone $100 to commit a murder vs $1,000,000 to commit a murder is likely going to affect the likelihood of the hit man agreeing to take a job, it\u2019s still murder (morally and legally) in either case though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Gaming nerds like us sometimes wish it were otherwise, but looks do matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T22:31:35-07:00","id":1460501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460498#post1460498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to take these sorts of online claims with a grain of salt. Anyone over a forum can claim to be a psychologist or be using a different definition of &amp;quot;psychologist&amp;quot; than I'm using.<br /> <br /> One of my friends recently expressed, and it's also been my own experience, that most cheating isn't spontaneous. Cheating tends to happen with people who spend time together and establish an emotional connection, vice a spontaneous &amp;quot;I'ma hit that.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> But when the latter kind of cheating happens, it tends to be with more attractive people. People are more likely to spontaneously cheat on their partners with an attractive alternative (or to get an attractive person to cheat on their partner) than a nonattractive one. We're also more predisposed to want to spend time around attractive people and develop the emotional connections that lead to affairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I neither believe nor disbelieve claims of expertise made on the Internet, since I consider the truthfulness of such claims to be irrelevant. Whether one is the top specialist in field or dropped out of the 3rd grade, the evidence they provide is what matters.<br /> <br /> Of course, physical attraction and the looks of the potential partner are just two of the many complex factors involved in infidelity, or indeed selecting sexual partners at all. I could have instead of saying a married man being flirted with, a could say that there was a woman whose devout religious beliefs require her to be a virgin until marriage, then how likely she is to violate that principle is based on an ugly socially awkward homeless man hitting on her versus a super handsome movie star.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m overweight and I struggle with dieting. I can certainly say that when I am on a diet or doing intermittent fasting, that the difficulty for my Self Control roll to resist food is higher for yummy food than bland food. Not being an alcoholic, though, I automatically resist that without a roll.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is not only a tangent but a controversial one, so maybe I\u2019ll just agree to disagree on the cheating topic and go back to vampire morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T02:39:47-07:00","id":1460504,"title":"","content":"Are we really discussing if the chance to be unfaithful is higher with a flirting person that you find attractive than one that you don't find attractive?<br /> <br /> Edit: Have read the first and third article (second one isn't possible due to security concerns) and there are no such claims or implications. Your interpretation of studies seem to be extremly selective and therefore biased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","user":"Ignithas","date":". 09-20-2021, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T05:29:14-07:00","id":1460514,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please avoid making sweeping statements about gender essentialism and what biological drives to cheat or not here. It's drifted into off-topic too.<br /> <br /> Just a warning.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T06:03:15-07:00","id":1460518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460498#post1460498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to take these sorts of online claims with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is right. My claims are less to stipulate that I'm an expert (something I can't prove), and more to hint that being more careful with &quot;your&quot; sources may be wise. I may be lying, exaggerating, and even be completely honest and still be wrong, but if I'm making such claims I'm either prepared to back my assertions with data or am badly needing to be put on my place.<br /> <br /> Hence I linked actual articles and other sources in my post. They're the actual experts for all purposes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460498#post1460498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when the latter kind of cheating happens, it tends to be with more attractive people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it does. The difference is between cause and direction.<br /> <br /> Does the cheating happen because it is with an attractive person, or once you're prone to cheating you'll direct yourself to an attractive person? The current body of research points to the latter.<br /> <br /> Spontaneous cheating is covered directly by some of those links, including the two articles, and the predictive patterns are all present on the cheater before exposure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1460501#post1460501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, this is not only a tangent but a controversial one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of that is my point. The problem isn't the belief in itself, but its place in a lot of other discourse structures. What I said earlier wasn't that your example was bad for the topic, but that it was offensive. And by the sheer number of <i>likes</i> we're both getting on what should by all means be considered a stupid tangent, we can see how much this question stirs people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T07:22:49-07:00","id":1460524,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Further conversation on it will result in infractions. Drop it guys.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T00:50:38-07:00","id":1460623,"title":"","content":"People with power are bad enough. Combine that with an essential need to do others harm...<br /> <br /> My vampires are people first. Their environment and difficult circumstances gives them a few sociopathic tendencies, and indeed vampires tend to embrace people who are already willing to screw others over to help themselves, but they're mostly very capable of positive relationships. Despite the so-called Jyhad, vampires cooperate and support eachother more often than they go against one another, and this is especially true in smaller cities. Most of their issues are felt more by mortals than other vampires. Vampires actually try to kill off the extremes, the super nice and the super evil. The two are risks in their own ways. Even in the Sabbat, someone who's drank the kool aid a little too much threatens the rest of the Sabbat either directly or through attracting attention. Vampires may want to shake the pot occasionally out of boredom, but natural selection favours those who crave stability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T22:55:06-07:00","id":1461160,"title":"","content":"Overall, pretty awful. As the sire of one of the PCs in my Northwest by Night chronicle put it: &quot;never become attached to your herd or retainers. Don't hesitate to sacrifice them if necessary. We are eternal; the kine are not.&quot; Elder vamps see people as playthings and resources at best, with the exceptions who have held onto their humanity (or walk one of the more benign Paths) being rare as owl's teeth. Ancillae at least affect the same attitudes, and many of them (not bound for a long unlife as these things are reckoned) have descended into depths of monstrosity. And no matter how vile a vampire may behave, as long as they keep the Traditions, they are not to be interfered with. The Camarilla countenances downright sadistic behavior: from the Toreador who raises up mortal artists and celebrities only to leave their lives in ruins once she moves on, to the Ventrue who controls the city's sex trade. As long as these Kindred respect the rules of <i>vampiric</i> society, they are treated as Solid Citizens of the Domain, even enjoying Title and high Prestation. When I set out to create my World of Darkness I wanted the PCs to feel that there's no Big Good for them to simply bank on. If they want to resist their Beasts, they'll have to find that wherewithal within themselves and be resourceful if they want to leave the city better than they found it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T23:33:06-07:00","id":1461166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires#post1460237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Storyteller has their own preferences for how they like to portray being a monster. &quot;Personal Horror&quot; was the byline of the original game with the idea the player characters would portray a reluctant monster that was horrified by the actions they might undertake under the influence of either the Beast or the Hunger. Some fans HATE Personal Horror. They prefer to play monsters who revel in their vampiric power or hate the idea of feeling guilt over feeding on what nature clearly intended as their food.<br /> <br /> Others have a preference for vampires who are different sort of monster who prey upon the evil doer and are more Nick Knight or Angel than cursed monster.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/forever_knight.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This is mostly about PCs, though, when people typically discuss it. PCs are able to defy the nature of their curse far differently than the majority of vampires. This is more a thread about how bad you think vampires in general are and specific groups ranging from Clans, Camarilla, and so on. How high is the average vamp's Humanity? What does that really mean? How often do they become wights?<br /> <br /> A general all purpose discussion of how dark being one of the undead and their life is morally and ethically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I haven't played Vampire in decades, so I don't know very much about Discipline Combos, for example. The one thing that kind of bothered me was that most of the Disciplines could not Improve The World in any way or create anything of value. You could have a Ventrue using Presence and Dominate to organize a bunch of mortals toward some positive goal. The main ingredient that allows the goal to be achieved is the group of humans doing human labor. When I look at the most up to date list of Vampiric Disciplines, they (still) seem to be for:<br /> <br /> - Controlling Others, human or vampire<br /> - Stealth, Investigation<br /> - Winning Combat<br /> <br /> I know there will be someone who says something like, &quot;This Thaumaturgy Ritual makes a mountain appear.&quot;. You could use Celerity and Potence to do manual labor for the benefit of the human population, but how often does anyone do this? Generally, Vampire Disciplines are for some purpose to do with surviving, killing or undermining (like with Dementation) other Vampires and acquiring power over others. <br /> <br /> This nearly complete lack of blood-derived power to improve the world and the wide variety of powers applicable to self-interested competition informs the question, &quot;Am I going to be good or bad?&quot;. A new Vampire assessing the powers available to them isn't going to conclude that their function is to do good for others. They are going to be calculating how they can use these powers to uncover dirty secrets, eliminate competitors, hide, raise an army and climb up the undead hierarchy.<br /> <br /> If you are looking to do Worldbuilding to encourage PCs to play Vampires with positive, constructive goals, have a wide variety of Disciplines (not just niche combos) that are directly applicable to those goals. I know one might say that the challenge is to play the doomed hero trying to do their best despite being a creature that only subtracts from the world, but if we have arrived at a point where a large section of the player-base hate the core theme, creating Constructive Disciplines needs to be considered. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T04:09:41-07:00","id":1461321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461166#post1461166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't played Vampire in decades, so I don't know very much about Discipline Combos, for example. The one thing that kind of bothered me was that most of the Disciplines could not Improve The World in any way or create anything of value. You could have a Ventrue using Presence and Dominate to organize a bunch of mortals toward some positive goal. The main ingredient that allows the goal to be achieved is the group of humans doing human labor. When I look at the most up to date list of Vampiric Disciplines, they (still) seem to be for:<br /> <br /> - Controlling Others, human or vampire<br /> - Stealth, Investigation<br /> - Winning Combat<br /> <br /> I know there will be someone who says something like, &quot;This Thaumaturgy Ritual makes a mountain appear.&quot;. You could use Celerity and Potence to do manual labor for the benefit of the human population, but how often does anyone do this? Generally, Vampire Disciplines are for some purpose to do with surviving, killing or undermining (like with Dementation) other Vampires and acquiring power over others.<br /> <br /> This nearly complete lack of blood-derived power to improve the world and the wide variety of powers applicable to self-interested competition informs the question, &quot;Am I going to be good or bad?&quot;. A new Vampire assessing the powers available to them isn't going to conclude that their function is to do good for others. They are going to be calculating how they can use these powers to uncover dirty secrets, eliminate competitors, hide, raise an army and climb up the undead hierarchy.<br /> <br /> If you are looking to do Worldbuilding to encourage PCs to play Vampires with positive, constructive goals, have a wide variety of Disciplines (not just niche combos) that are directly applicable to those goals. I know one might say that the challenge is to play the doomed hero trying to do their best despite being a creature that only subtracts from the world, but if we have arrived at a point where a large section of the player-base hate the core theme, creating Constructive Disciplines needs to be considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to change the world/setting, you often do so via Backgrounds which are generated or at least enhanced by Disciplines.<br /> <br /> A coterie with each member at Resources 5 pooling everything into a communal slush fund is a very powerful group. Then have each member specialize there Contacts and Influence in different parts of society. Yes Dominate and Presence can be very useful, but in our modern world it is arguable that the Path of Technomancy is on par if not better in some scenarios.<br /> <br /> Then you just ensure that the right projects get funded, the wrong laws don't get passed. There was a book (pre-V20) talking about when a Prince is going to lose a city to the Sabbat that they would more or less &quot;fix up&quot; the city before leaving to make it much harder for the Sabbat to reside there. Allowing city maintenance to fix all the broken street lights, allowing the cops to go where ever they needed stop crime, add additional laws and requirements for any establishment open after dark that made for easy hunting, etc. Basically your coterie is doing this, but without it being a parting middle finger to some vampiric invaders.<br /> <br /> To be honest though, the Vampire setting breaks down horribly once you start thinking in terms of making changes. The Exalted game line on the other hand was built around the notion that the PCs would change the course of history on almost a by game basis. Playing V:tM with an Exalted mindset.... gets you labeled a munchkin of the highest order and tends to give many STs seizures since that play style more or less breaks the V:tM setting over your knee and trashes many of the conventions of the game.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, that is one of my favorite ways to play V:tM. When you have eternity as a starting point, it seems an utter waste to spend it doing little more than constantly scheming, rather than achieving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T06:56:01-07:00","id":1461326,"title":"","content":"Most of the NPC vampires in my campaign city hover around Humanity 4-5 unless they\u2019re under a century old (those are generally 5-6) or an aberration that proves the rule (there\u2019s a Nos with Humanity 8 who feeds only from animals and keeps no ghouls\u2026 he was once a monster, but got a wakeup call,<br /> found religion; the Cult of Osiris specifically; and has rebuilt his humanity over the last century and now seeks to \u201cbalance the scales\u201d before he goes and takes a sunbath).<br /> <br /> The PCs have higher Humanity scores listed than what I consider them to have (and the ones involved both have the blush of health and early riser merits too which basically makes degeneration irrelevant until they drop below a 5 where bearing and virtue caps can start to ding them so it\u2019s not worth the table fight that would result), owing mostly to these players really not giving any deep thought to their action. The short version is they started a blood donation center where volunteers can donate blood to help at the local children\u2019s hospital; except they\u2019re essentially embezzling a good chunk of the donations (to the tune of over a hundred pints a month for multiple vampires and their ghouls) for their own personal use, not just to sustain themselves, one of them is trying to become a pop diva using lots of presence at every performance and justifies burning off the extra blood that takes with the notion that part of the proceeds go to various charitable causes she supports. Having recently turned some of their long time ghouls into vampires they\u2019re also looking to blood bind a brand new batch of mortals in order to advance their interests (which are for the \u201cgreater good\u201d obviously).<br /> <br /> I dunno about anyone else, but I\u2019d consider stealing people\u2019s charitable donations for personal use, brainwashing people into buying tickets to your performances using said charitable donations and also planning to enslave people through addiction also using those stolen charitable donations to be rather monstrous even as they tell themselves they\u2019re being humane and even heroic.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s downright hilarious to me because they\u2019re all about what good people they are as they actively shun the few high humanity good NPCs (who make them uncomfortable when they try to get them to be better people) and sidling right up to some of the lowest Humanity ones (who praise their actions even as every last one is planning to backstab them as soon as they\u2019ve gotten what they wanted out of them). It\u2019s all going to blow up in their faces eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T10:26:00-07:00","id":1461355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461326#post1461326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the NPC vampires in my campaign city hover around Humanity 4-5 unless they\u2019re under a century old (those are generally 5-6) or an aberration that proves the rule (there\u2019s a Nos with Humanity 8 who feeds only from animals and keeps no ghouls\u2026 he was once a monster, but got a wakeup call,<br /> found religion; the Cult of Osiris specifically; and has rebuilt his humanity over the last century and now seeks to \u201cbalance the scales\u201d before he goes and takes a sunbath).<br /> <br /> The PCs have higher Humanity scores listed than what I consider them to have (and the ones involved both have the blush of health and early riser merits too which basically makes degeneration irrelevant until they drop below a 5 where bearing and virtue caps can start to ding them so it\u2019s not worth the table fight that would result), owing mostly to these players really not giving any deep thought to their action. The short version is they started a blood donation center where volunteers can donate blood to help at the local children\u2019s hospital; except they\u2019re essentially embezzling a good chunk of the donations (to the tune of over a hundred pints a month for multiple vampires and their ghouls) for their own personal use, not just to sustain themselves, one of them is trying to become a pop diva using lots of presence at every performance and justifies burning off the extra blood that takes with the notion that part of the proceeds go to various charitable causes she supports. Having recently turned some of their long time ghouls into vampires they\u2019re also looking to blood bind a brand new batch of mortals in order to advance their interests (which are for the \u201cgreater good\u201d obviously).<br /> <br /> I dunno about anyone else, but I\u2019d consider stealing people\u2019s charitable donations for personal use, brainwashing people into buying tickets to your performances using said charitable donations and also planning to enslave people through addiction also using those stolen charitable donations to be rather monstrous even as they tell themselves they\u2019re being humane and even heroic.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s downright hilarious to me because they\u2019re all about what good people they are as they actively shun the few high humanity good NPCs (who make them uncomfortable when they try to get them to be better people) and sidling right up to some of the lowest Humanity ones (who praise their actions even as every last one is planning to backstab them as soon as they\u2019ve gotten what they wanted out of them). It\u2019s all going to blow up in their faces eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like good roleplaying for degeneration, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T11:24:03-07:00","id":1461371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461326#post1461326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">them so it\u2019s not worth the table fight that would result</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the only problematic part for me in this. And is a hell of a big problem.<br /> <br /> Use the Sanctity rules, screw with the official WW party line on this. When they lose the benefits of their Merits just give then back the points to buy something else that makes sense. But don't stop holding them accountable for their actions.<br /> <br /> It is not just a matter of playing by the rules, but since you plan on having them eat their consequences with gusto then denying them Degeneration Rolls is denying them the very mechanic in the game that shows, don't tell, that they're screwing up. When things go down they'll be upset and will be right in being so, because the lack of Degeneration is proof in itself that they did nothing wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T17:16:48-07:00","id":1461440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461321#post1461321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to change the world/setting, you often do so via Backgrounds which are generated or at least enhanced by Disciplines.<br /> <br /> A coterie with each member at Resources 5 pooling everything into a communal slush fund is a very powerful group. Then have each member specialize there Contacts and Influence in different parts of society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resources and Contacts are not specific to the vampiric form or condition. A bunch of mortals could do the same. When a Toreador artist creates something, they are relying primarily on Attributes and Abilities that a mortal artist can possess. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461321#post1461321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes Dominate and Presence can be very useful, but in our modern world it is arguable that the Path of Technomancy is on par if not better in some scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Path of Technomancy allow the Vampire to improve the function of the machine he's controlling? Is there another Disciple that facilitates building machines in the first place? I suppose the Vampire could buy a Rapid Prototyping Machine and build out a life sustaining complex that humans could live in where they would recover easily from blood loss from the Coterie's feeding. A kind of self-contained hive. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461321#post1461321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you just ensure that the right projects get funded, the wrong laws don't get passed. There was a book (pre-V20) talking about when a Prince is going to lose a city to the Sabbat that they would more or less &quot;fix up&quot; the city before leaving to make it much harder for the Sabbat to reside there. Allowing city maintenance to fix all the broken street lights, allowing the cops to go where ever they needed stop crime, add additional laws and requirements for any establishment open after dark that made for easy hunting, etc. Basically your coterie is doing this, but without it being a parting middle finger to some vampiric invaders.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Prince bit is kind of funny. Princes maintain a state of affairs where the street lights stay broken, police are barred from certain areas and can't properly investigate crime to facilitate Vampires' needs and only take action to improve life for the mortal population when forced to retreat - &quot;My city is trash, as it should be. Sabbat on the way? The mortals deserve better!&quot;. <br /> <br /> I remember a Chronicle where my character laundered money for a drug kingpin and then used Dominate 3 to erase his and his accountants' memory of the scheme. I pulled connections to have him audited so that he was made to testify that he did not have any assets beyond what I had left him with, permanently forgoing any chance to recover his wealth. He was receiving tips from crooked cops about informants in his gangs. I rewrote his memory so he believed some of his most loyal thugs had been acquired by police and that the actual informants were the people to who he should delegate the task of housecleaning. I used his drug pyramid like a vacuum cleaner to pull in every lowlife wannabe willing to carry out violence for the chance to join, all of them boasting past crimes into cameras and microphones. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461321#post1461321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest though, the Vampire setting breaks down horribly once you start thinking in terms of making changes. The Exalted game line on the other hand was built around the notion that the PCs would change the course of history on almost a by game basis. Playing V:tM with an Exalted mindset.... gets you labeled a munchkin of the highest order and tends to give many STs seizures since that play style more or less breaks the V:tM setting over your knee and trashes many of the conventions of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire is: Tragic (maybe)Hero. Exalted has this &quot;Chosen Ones&quot; vibe, from what I understand. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461321#post1461321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Needless to say, that is one of my favorite ways to play V:tM. When you have eternity as a starting point, it seems an utter waste to spend it doing little more than constantly scheming, rather than achieving.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you could assign the role of Doomed Character to the players' Sires. The player-Progeny have been Embraced so they can right the wrongs caused by their Sires' Degeneration. Of course, scheming PCs might just exploit the older Vampires' guilt for personal advancement.\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T17:19:56-07:00","id":1461441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461371#post1461371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the only problematic part for me in this. And is a hell of a big problem.<br /> <br /> Use the Sanctity rules, screw with the official WW party line on this. When they lose the benefits of their Merits just give then back the points to buy something else that makes sense. But don't stop holding them accountable for their actions.<br /> <br /> It is not just a matter of playing by the rules, but since you plan on having them eat their consequences with gusto then denying them Degeneration Rolls is denying them the very mechanic in the game that shows, don't tell, that they're screwing up. When things go down they'll be upset and will be right in being so, because the lack of Degeneration is proof in itself that they did nothing wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) there\u2019s no reason they should lose those merits; it\u2019s not like they require a specific Humanity score to function; indeed Blush of Health isn\u2019t even worth taking if you think you can hold Humanity 8+ and Light Sleeper is similarly less useful the higher your Humanity.<br /> <br /> B) One issue was when to even have them make a Degeneration check and how often should it be repeated if they pull off the first one. When they set up the LLC? The first embezzled blood bag they guzzled? Just one check (if you can rationalize it the first time with the intent of repeating should the original rationalization hold)? Every blood bag? Every ten? Only the vampires who actually came up with the scheme or the ones who got blood bags as a gift without questioning the source?<br /> <br /> Likewise, if I get too sticky on this I\u2019d realistically have to require a degeneration check every time a vampire takes a blood point by deceit in a nightclub\u2026 because I can see the argument that the blood bank embezzling is no worse than stealing blood during a make out session in a dark alcove could argue this is no different and also eliminates any accidental overfeeding risk so is arguably more moral.<br /> <br /> C) Related to when to do degeneration checks; they haven\u2019t actually started ghouling yet because they\u2019re still looking for candidates. The Embracing was, in one case, of a ghoul well past his mortal lifespan and had accumulated flaws like light sensitivity and their domitor\u2019s clan flaw. The other was spur of the moment as they had been poisoned by an enemy of the Sire-to-be and was moments from death when they drained him and fed him in an effort to \u201csave\u201d him. I DO plan on making them check for degeneration on that unless they are utterly upfront about the consequences of the third drink with whichever candidates are picked.<br /> <br /> D) The consequences that will bite them has nothing directly to do with degeneration; it\u2019s the company they chose to keep\u2026 the ones who appeared charming and seemed like friends who would do favors without any obvious benefit to themselves by doing so that they started trusting without question. These are vampires and when one of these guys came to them with a warning of another vampire plotting against the PC and advised the PCs to strike first; they didn\u2019t even question it\u2026 they just started making plans as if it were true.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not something them getting degeneration checks for the blood bank is going to alert them to; but it\u2019s more a case of their being unable to recognize that charm, wealth, power and glamour have nothing to do with whether you\u2019re a monster or not.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can only do so much if they ignore obvious signs. I literally had a thin-blooded seer break into a prophetic trance where they screamed out \u201cBeware the Bronze Man; he brings ruin for us all!\u201d in front of them and then, at Elysium, an extremely attractive Mediterranean vampire with bronzy skin presented himself to the Prince as a goodwill ambassador from the Assamites as the schismatics negotiated for entry.<br /> <br /> All the warnings went right out the window at the description of his smoldering brown eyes, square jaw and muscles and he became a trusted confidant (the one who gave them the \u201cwarning\u201d of the vampire plotting against them actually). Why? Because he was \u201chot\u201d and the de facto leader of the PC coiterie was envisioning her Anita Blake novels.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not deliberately out to get them, but they have somehow systematically picked the worst of the worst among the NPCs as the \u201cgood people\u201d they can trust (invariably the elites of vampire society) while distrusting every last NPC who\u2019s tried to warn them of how scheming and evil their associates are. At some point the bill comes due.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T21:58:03-07:00","id":1461480,"title":"","content":"With a big embezzlement like this I would make a case of rolling for Degeneration every now and them when they're presented with reminders of what they're doing and, more importantly, the ridiculous scale. At Humanity 7 Theft is a sin, at 8 the accidental injury of another. At 6 I concede that only the eventual death of someone due to the lack of resources they're embezzling would do it. It is the difference between &quot;blood as a part of someone's health&quot; and &quot;blood as a measurable resource to save lives at a medical facility&quot;, and the scale of the thing.<br /> <br /> But it was more the way you mentioned &quot;not worth the table fight that would result&quot; that I misinterpreted. I'm a bit worried that this may come to be an unproductive frustration, but if those aren't new players then by all means go ahead and screw them to your heart's content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T00:21:47-07:00","id":1461494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461440#post1461440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resources and Contacts are not specific to the vampiric form or condition. A bunch of mortals could do the same. When a Toreador artist creates something, they are relying primarily on Attributes and Abilities that a mortal artist can possess.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they are an Elder vampire with 6+ dot stat blocks, they are using the same mortal traits to create that art. Disciplines are the obvious thing that makes the difference between mortals and vampires, but I would say that the vampiric ability to have plans that can reach from the multi-decade to the multi-century level is what makes the biggest difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461440#post1461440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Path of Technomancy allow the Vampire to improve the function of the machine he's controlling? Is there another Disciple that facilitates building machines in the first place? I suppose the Vampire could buy a Rapid Prototyping Machine and build out a life sustaining complex that humans could live in where they would recover easily from blood loss from the Coterie's feeding. A kind of self-contained hive.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to go full technology powerhouse, you use Path of Conjuring to create any tech hardware that is currently in existence, even the in development stuff. Then you use Path of Technomancy to hack the planet essentially. Part of this really comes down to the fact that WW never did proper rules for what a mortal hacker could do, so the thaumaturgy path is a bit weird. If you have an IRL understanding of cyber security or even just some hacking basics, most of the path gets broken real fast.<br /> <br /> So in the example of a self sustained vampire hive, you would use Path of Conjuring to fabricate the supplies or parts to build the hive and maintain it. Then you use the Path of Technomancy to hack blood banks to send fresh deliveries on a regular basis. After that the Path of Technomancy becomes your long range weapon of choice to manipulate stock markets, change property records, fabricate email leaks, generate endless money through bank hacking, etc.<br /> <br /> It might not be exciting, but in truth a Coterie could just purchase a decommissioned missile silo and have it converted into a private vampire fortress/luxury apartments/vampire hive in the middle of no where and hack most of the country. Normally this would leave them open to tracing or back hacking, except Path of Technomancy allows you to connect to the internet without using hardware so no IP address and no signal trace.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461440#post1461440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire is: Tragic (maybe)Hero. Exalted has this &quot;Chosen Ones&quot; vibe, from what I understand.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest I have always felt that the need for Vampire to be angsty and tragic is a very teenage thing. I always liked the idea of being comfortable with ones monster side and simply going on with unlife. Or to put it another way, Vampire was really designed to be the Lost Boys (street level/personal interactions), rather than empire building or big picture influence peddling. Then again I haven't been a teenage for decades, so perhaps I am the wrong demographic for the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T00:56:53-07:00","id":1461498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461494#post1461494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest I have always felt that the need for Vampire to be angsty and tragic is a very teenage thing. I always liked the idea of being comfortable with ones monster side and simply going on with unlife. Or to put it another way, Vampire was really designed to be the Lost Boys (street level/personal interactions), rather than empire building or big picture influence peddling. Then again I haven't been a teenage for decades, so perhaps I am the wrong demographic for the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>My 40 year perspective on Vampire 5th Edition is that it's a game about regrets and frustrations as well as guilt. A vampire makes a lot of compromises to live in Camarilla and/or Anarch society and also looks back at his past with some perspective on the past. It was very good for my teenage years but as a middle aged man, I also like it as a story about the long perspective and the changes that actually work well with the metaplot.<br /> <br /> I grew up in a very fundamentalist hardcore reactionary household then went into liberal activism with an anarchist tinge and later became an author. Your average vampire will go through much more trying to navigate vampire society as a Fledgling to Ancilla with no &quot;right&quot; answer other than survival.<br /> <br /> But, of course, vampire is whatever you want it to be. It's after all, just a game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:22:34-07:00","id":1461505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461166#post1461166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing that kind of bothered me was that most of the Disciplines could not Improve The World in any way or create anything of value.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that the title question is affected by their power spread. Destruction is always easier than Creation, even for humans, but the question is about how NPCs in general behave and that depends on the many factors of how the ST see vampiric society. The lack of supernatural powers to create lasting good seems like weak reason to conclude they're going to be bad people, too simplistic.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> Disciplines that can be used for good, like creating art, doing productive work or even helping with healing include: Animalism, Auspex, Chimerstry, Vicissitude, Melpominee, Ogham, Temporis, Valeren and Visceratika. They're not geared toward creation or positive uses, but are particularly easy to use positively with just a modicum of creativity.<br /> <br /> Disciplines that have outright positive uses in the sense of the creation of something new and lasting or other beneficial effects: Bardo, Obeah, Spiritus and every sorcery discipline (Necromancy, Thaumaturgy, Dur-An-Ki, Koldunic Sorcery, Akhu, Nahuallotl, Sadhana and Wanga).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:54:04-07:00","id":1461519,"title":"","content":"I think vampires using their powers to &quot;help&quot; people is one of those things that is going to be an essential part of their storytelling at least as part of what V:TM does. The question is whether or not that is going to work out. Sometimes it will, sometimes it won't. One of the more understated stories in VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE: BLOODLINES is that there's a &quot;serial killer&quot; operating in the area that turns out to be a Gangrel Neonate.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://vtmb.fandom.com/wiki/Southland_Slasher\" target=\"_blank\">https://vtmb.fandom.com/wiki/Southland_Slasher</a><br /> <br /> He's been on a killing spree after the guys who did a car jacking and proceeded to kill his family. After you manage to confront him and calm him down a bit, he basically says that he killed everyone involved in the murder of his family. Now he plans to basically go full Punisher and continue killing people who are &quot;evil.&quot; Now the game doesn't bother to explain this or lecture you but it's fairly clear that killing all those people has messed with this guys head. You may be able to wipe out 100+ people in the game and not go insane from it (or maybe you're already insane as the kind of person who has killed 100+ people) but the experience has left him in a bad mental space.<br /> <br /> If he keeps doing this, he will be lost to the Beast because it's only made him angrier and nastier.<br /> <br /> You as a vampire must encourage him to drop his crusade to be a vigilante and try to do something else with his unlife. I always liked that because it added a bit of dirt and muck on what might have otherwise been a more justified story in another game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-26-2021, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T09:27:10-07:00","id":1461562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461480#post1461480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it was more the way you mentioned &quot;not worth the table fight that would result&quot; that I misinterpreted. I'm a bit worried that this may come to be an unproductive frustration, but if those aren't new players then by all means go ahead and screw them to your heart's content.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, basically it\u2019s not worth the fight with people over a fun activity with people who in their heads are playing out something from the Anita Blake novels. Just like it\u2019s not worth telling them that, as a WoD vampire their character has little interest in sex beyond as a feeding strategy or that everyone she meets isn\u2019t actually a model (I finish a description of an NPC and she dives onto her phone to find a pic for them and it is invariably some 20-30 something model\u2026 in her head we\u2019re playing in the world of a CW drama series). Another one spends all their time planning their latest \u201clook at me\u201d performance and always wants to know whar the current status of YouTube hits, Instagram likes and Patreon followers they have.<br /> <br /> So if most of the reason they\u2019re here is for the fantasy of wealth, power and privilege, I\u2019m not going to fight it\u2026 all their coming consequences are from trying to lead that lifestyle among backstabbing sociopaths (i.e. vampires) anyway and the odds of them actually dropping to 4 or less where it might begin to have a mechanical bearing are pretty slim. So mostly I\u2019ve decided to just keep a running tally on where I think their actual Humanity falls for my own edification on what the slide down the humanity scale looks like when you don\u2019t have a metagaming mechanic to let you know you\u2019re sliding off the rails\u2026 because really, the character has no way of knowing what their Humanity score is (nor would they see it as a score).<br /> <br /> Right now I peg them at 6 (the level you no longer check for theft) and that may be adjusted depending on how forthright they are with their ghoul candidates about what it actually entails (if the candidates have informed consent on the blood bond then I don\u2019t think there\u2019s a check needed if they\u2019re already at 6; some people would make that deal anyway for a variety of reasons).<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll have them roll if bodies start dropping in the consequences stage (and there my decision to use the DAV20 degeneration rules with difficulty based on the gap between the sin and your present rating could smooth out the discrepancy as they would expect to fail on such rolls where the difficulty would be 9+), but otherwise I\u2019ll just let the \u201cexperiment\u201d run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 09-26-2021, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T12:45:23-07:00","id":1461593,"title":"","content":"Again, if they're new players then I'm not totally on the same page, but its your game, you're not doing anything I wouldn't to my regulars (that are very experienced players that enjoy the downs of their characters as much as the ups or even more). I don't dig some judgement on the players' fantasies either, an RPG is a power fantasy anyway, but at least you're not doing it on their faces and saying they're playing wrong. Seen that kind of shitty behavior before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T13:39:25-07:00","id":1461606,"title":"","content":"Eh, I don't think it's an issue if the players just accept they're assholes and having fun being so either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T14:34:39-07:00","id":1461615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461593#post1461593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, if they're new players then I'm not totally on the same page, but its your game, you're not doing anything I wouldn't to my regulars (that are very experienced players that enjoy the downs of their characters as much as the ups or even more). I don't dig some judgement on the players' fantasies either, an RPG is a power fantasy anyway, but at least you're not doing it on their faces and saying they're playing wrong. Seen that kind of shitty behavior before.</div> </div> </div> </div>To qualify, they\u2019re experienced at RPGs in general (the newest has been gaming for a decade), but they know VtM mostly via the influence it\u2019s had on the urban fantasy genre in general and one in particular has a particular affection for Anita Blake novels.<br /> <br /> I also don\u2019t mind the power fantasy element; it\u2019s just their insistence of their PCs\u2019 moral righteousness as they do it that just makes them come off as utterly lacking in self-awareness and is irksome primarily because I feel like they\u2019re going to be blindsided and upset when all their vampire \u201cfriends\u201d drop them like garbage as soon as they\u2019ve gotten what they wanted out of them.<br /> <br /> I mean\u2026 they\u2019re VAMPIRES! The Prince and Primogen using younger vampires in their schemes and discarding them as soon as they\u2019re no longer useful is Vampire 101. The few moral NPCs have been warning them that they\u2019re just being used; but they refuse to listen because it runs contrary to their self-narrative of being beloved members of the elite.<br /> <br /> If they at least implied this was just the attitude of their PCs and they understood what\u2019s going on I could handle it fine; but it seems to be the player perspective and that\u2019s just\u2026 What\u2019s a Storyteller to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 09-26-2021, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T14:35:58-07:00","id":1461616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461606#post1461606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I don't think it's an issue if the players just accept they're assholes and having fun being so either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me neither, I'm just worried 'cause their players don't seem to actually accept or even acknowledge that. Again, I'm worried about new players, not old ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T15:00:01-07:00","id":1461620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461615#post1461615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">makes them come off as utterly lacking in self-awareness and is irksome primarily because I feel like they\u2019re going to be blindsided and upset when all their vampire \u201cfriends\u201d drop them like garbage as soon as they\u2019ve gotten what they wanted out of them.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> What\u2019s a Storyteller to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest that you talk to them about the issue out-of-character. Not including actual story details, of course, but talk to them straight and clearly.<br /> <br /> Be sure that they know the game is about a corrupted society, even if some of its members aren't so bad, that some NPC's may lie to them and stab them in the back, that vampiric secrecy is deadly serious and that they generally occupy an &quot;evil illuminatti&quot; role on society.<br /> <br /> Use the embezzlement as an asset here. It gives you something you can discuss with them outside of the game what they think about it versus what it really is. You surely don't have to tell them that they shouldn't do it, but just be sure that they understand what it is and that this is relevant in the game.<br /> <br /> Ask them directly how they'll feel if some character they trust betrays them. They may surprise you being chill about it, but parse first all the NPCs to make it clear that any character at all can betray them for reasons they may not be seeing at the moment and that they're thinking it through.<br /> <br /> Finally, weigh in the value of changing the game a bit. If after all that your players say they'll be ok, and then they don't, its on them, they're consenting adults after all. But if an open conversation shows that you should adapt yourself and adjust the setting to be more Blake-like, go for it. Your time with this group of real people is far more important than the game's purity.<br /> <br /> Not saying any of this lightly, I know this sometimes happen and even with experienced players this is a tough situation, but sometimes an outside perspective helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T15:01:39-07:00","id":1461621,"title":"","content":"Also, if they just want to be a bunch of grifting assholes, be fine with that too I think.<br /> <br /> Because if you're going to be a vampire, be a vampire.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T17:22:42-07:00","id":1461627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461498#post1461498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My 40 year perspective on Vampire 5th Edition is that it's a game about regrets and frustrations as well as guilt. A vampire makes a lot of compromises to live in Camarilla and/or Anarch society and also looks back at his past with some perspective on the past. It was very good for my teenage years but as a middle aged man, I also like it as a story about the long perspective and the changes that actually work well with the metaplot.<br /> <br /> I grew up in a very fundamentalist hardcore reactionary household then went into liberal activism with an anarchist tinge and later became an author. Your average vampire will go through much more trying to navigate vampire society as a Fledgling to Ancilla with no &quot;right&quot; answer other than survival.<br /> <br /> But, of course, vampire is whatever you want it to be. It's after all, just a game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, a fellow 4th decade fossil. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In my case, I could probably be classified as the flip side of the coin. My parents were world travelers during 60s &amp; 70s, the family ran an antiques business. So every different way of doing things or belief system is greeted with the same shrug of indifference and a quick review of if it works better than what is currently being used.<br /> <br /> If there was a market for it, we sold it. Yes I did bring a shrunken human head to show and tell back in the 3rd grade (the 80s were so much more relaxed about human remains). We would work with churches to appraise items left to them all the while working with insurance companies to review claims. This sort of background makes for a historically well informed if some what Eternal ST, but oddly makes the Elder vampires more relatable to me than the neonates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T18:46:41-07:00","id":1461787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461505#post1461505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that the title question is affected by their power spread. Destruction is always easier than Creation, even for humans, but the question is about how NPCs in general behave and that depends on the many factors of how the ST see vampiric society. The lack of supernatural powers to create lasting good seems like weak reason to conclude they're going to be bad people, too simplistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I focused narrowly on Disciplines to add something to the discussion where others had commented in different aspects of Vampirism. If you want another example, I would say that The Camarilla's Masquerade necessitates a lot of institutional fuckery that has disastrous consequences for society. For practically every major institution, there is a Declared Mandate and a Hidden Function carried out on behalf of Vampire overlords that are in conflict.<br /> <br /> The local police department is the simplest example. A group of teenagers are messing around after dark and trespassing in a seemingly abandoned place. A high status Vampire who considers this his territory frenzies and kills the intruders. The growling and screaming attracts attention and the Vampire is forced to flee before he can drag away the bodies. The police respond and have the duty of informing the families of these kids that they were murdered. They promise to find the killer.<br /> <br /> The high status vampire visits the Prince, making apologies and excuses. The Prince exerts his already established power over the police department, turning the investigation into a coverup. Imagine what this does to the police officers who swore to grieving parents they would catch the killer. Now they are framing some poor socially awkward man for the rampage.<br /> <br /> The Declared Mandate of the police department, to protect citizens, investigate crime and arrest criminals, is totally undermined by the Hidden Function, keeping Vampires safe from scrutiny, which takes priority. When people do not believe in institutions they pay taxes for and have to obey, they turn to often worse alternatives, like Vampiric blood cults or straight forward radicalism. All new Vampires are drawn from this hopeless mortal population, adding to the problem.<br /> <br /> An even more basic and important institution, The Family, is undermined by the creation of Ghouls. Let's say that the captain of the police force is a married man. His wife is proud of his dedication and bravery. They love each other. They have kids old enough to understand things they overhear or see in the news. Along comes a sexy female Ventrue Primogen who blood-bonds the police captain. Now, he is more deeply in love with this Vampire than he ever was with his wife. On top of that, she is having him carry out a Hidden Function of covering up Vampires' crimes. This is going to have an erosive influence on the captain, as a person, and his family.<br /> <br /> It's not so much that individual Vampires are all bad. It's that, collectively, they cannot help but be extremely bad for human society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461505#post1461505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also:<br /> <br /> Disciplines that can be used for good, like creating art, doing productive work or even helping with healing include: Animalism, Auspex, Chimerstry, Vicissitude, Melpominee, Ogham, Temporis, Valeren and Visceratika. They're not geared toward creation or positive uses, but are particularly easy to use positively with just a modicum of creativity.<br /> <br /> Disciplines that have outright positive uses in the sense of the creation of something new and lasting or other beneficial effects: Bardo, Obeah, Spiritus and every sorcery discipline (Necromancy, Thaumaturgy, Dur-An-Ki, Koldunic Sorcery, Akhu, Nahuallotl, Sadhana and Wanga).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish there were an obvious alternative to Whitewolf Wiki that would turn up in the searches. Okay, so I won't try to nitpick this list. Some Vampires have Disciplines that can be used for the benefit of humans and other Vampires. They can easily be Good. Is there a kind of underground economy of services exchanged between Vampires with these powers and humans who would benefit in the current setting? I could see an alternative to creating Ghouls. Pay mortals to do things Vampires need done during the day with money raised from Constructive Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 09-27-2021, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T18:06:29-07:00","id":1462192,"title":"","content":"In my games you lose humanity for doing vampiric stuff that makes you be more disconected from your superego (humanity) and more near of the ego (beast)<br /> <br /> It isnt about being good or bad becuase humanity is able of both while the beast is not a moral being but rather pure instinct.<br /> <br /> For this reason a vampire killing someone to archive something isn\u00b4t going degenerate unless he did it against his personal code, but if he kills someone during a frenzy or while feeding then he rolls for degeneration not becuase what he did was wrong or right but becuase the lose of control.<br /> <br /> Learning disciplines, embracing, creating ghoul etc... are all vampiric acts so indulging in them also causes degeneration wich is why as players and vampires age they become less human.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><i>The more you take from the beast...the more the beast takes from you</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T16:31:48-07:00","id":1462348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1461615#post1461615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they at least implied this was just the attitude of their PCs and they understood what\u2019s going on I could handle it fine; but it seems to be the player perspective and that\u2019s just\u2026 What\u2019s a Storyteller to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fuck' em in the ear. You've already warned them OOC. They should know by now.<br /> <br /> But it sounds like so far they are reacting to the rewards you (the ST) have been giving them through the NPCs. So they're just acting on the carrots you've trained them to accept. (Players can be oblivious. In one LARP I had an NPC that I told everyone up front had the Untrustworthy x3 characteristic. But he acted very nice to people, was willing to help out in minor ways, and had enough power and prestige he could be a useful associate. One PC found him too useful and began thinking that NPC was his friend and ally. So I waited for the right moment and then the NPC did something that directly harmed the PC. He was shocked and started hating the NPC. He couldn't believe it. The other players had to remind him that the NPC was always said to have Untrustworthy x3 so why did he ever trust him? Of course, most of them were doing something similar with that NPC. They started changing their behavior though once they saw what happened to the first PC. People always learn better through experience than talk. Only after the LARP PCs actually saw that NPC do something that demonstrated that Untrustworthy x3 trait did they really know that the NPC was in fact untrustworthy.)<br /> <br /> So you need one of those NPCs who likes them so much and is such a good friend to betray them.<br /> <br /> Now there's some guidelines on how to do that. First, it should be fairly minor. You want the PCs to be able to recover from said betrayal, not put them so far down the hole the players get discouraged and give up. Second, the betrayal needs to make sense. The NPCs needs to benefit more from his betrayal than he is giving up by burning his relationship with the NPC (otherwise it is just stupid and makes no sense. The PCs must see that the NPC benefited from the action). You just need to figure that out.<br /> <br /> Once it has happened once, they should be much more wary of the other NPCs and reset expectations.<br /> <br /> However, if they still act naive, then that's a signal to the other vampire NPCs that the coterie is stupid and can be exploited. Better to use them now before they're used up and useless. So if they continue, have them start meeting a lot of new &quot;friends.&quot; And after some time, these friends have a problem they need some help with. They should catch on soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T19:02:05-07:00","id":1462377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460237-world-building-how-bad-are-your-vampires?p=1462348#post1462348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one LARP I had an NPC that I told everyone up front had the Untrustworthy x3 characteristic. But he acted very nice to people, was willing to help out in minor ways, and had enough power and prestige he could be a useful associate. One PC found him too useful and began thinking that NPC was his friend and ally. So I waited for the right moment and then the NPC did something that directly harmed the PC. He was shocked and started hating the NPC. He couldn't believe it. The other players had to remind him that the NPC was always said to have Untrustworthy x3 so why did he ever trust him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Similarly, one thing that always cracked me up when I was in the thick of playing was that the other PCs treated my main character as if he were a paragon of virtue largely because he was courteous and reliable. He was a centuries-old Tzimisce warlord\u2014he took keeping his word very seriously once it was given, and following proper etiquette was ingrained behavior. But he was also ruthless and unconcerned with collateral damage, which resulted in PCs deaths when they stumbled into his solution to a gathering of enemies despite his warning. He didn't let the fact that several allies were at risk stop him from pursuing his goal, or even slow the hand that lit the fuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T18:33:43-07:00","id":1463038,"title":"","content":"Some 'nice' or likable NPC vampires from various games I've been in or run<br /> <br /> Sabbat Bishop Elizibeth of clan lasombra and her warpack.<br /> Bishop of silence (Her job was to maintain masquarade in a Sabbat stonghold), she was very supportive of younger vampires and subordinates, doted on her childe and maintained what she called an &quot;animal wellfare&quot; attitude towards humans were she was comfortable using killing or exploiting humans but avoided harming without reason and explicitly avoided pety acts of sadism. She was genrally relaxed and affable in person. Her personal warpack were called the scream queens and were fiercly loyal to one another effectively she slowly embraced her human friends if and when they were struggling in life. Combined with the Vaulderie they had about as pleasent a relationship in the Sabbat as you can get.<br /> Her 'scary' side was her tenacity in killing people who crossed or challanged her she once quiped/implied threat &quot;you know you might want to consider the reason everyone currently alive likes me might not just because of my good looks and charm.....&quot; what really threw people off was her tendancy to personally come and kill them herself, considering she's a lasombra warpack veteran this was a very real threat.<br /> <br /> Ventrue Harpy Molly (matilda of beumont)<br /> 900 year old eldar, once had a key mission for an up and coming pack from a city to ensure the safety of a ancient portrait in transport to her haven. A causal conversation after getting the portrait was of her long dead husband and daughter, the subtext implied she both desired to be with them again but was increasingly burdened by the idea they'd fear and despise what she'd become. She became kinder and thoughtful in the following years eventually stepping down from harpy to become primogen.<br /> <br /> 'prince' stevan smith-Borderline autarkis on a small town usa, he runs a night radio show and hadnt killed anyone since 1972. Probably caitiff or Gangrel<br /> <br /> Hecata/Cappaodocian Constantinianus the hagiographer. Recently awoken Cappaodician, strong advocate of restoring the ashen priesthood and currently preaching the road of humanity/greek orthodoxy to the Caitiff, thinbloods and anyone who listens. Secretly seeking Golconda.<br /> <br /> Jenny-tzmisce body mod enthusiast and tatooist. Jenny, runs a back door body mod parlor where she discretly provided surgery when she thinks she can get away we with it. Takes guest rights very seriously and never oversteps the boundries","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-08-2021, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T21:41:39-07:00","id":1463055,"title":"","content":"Is this just something that hits you when it's September? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-your-kindred</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T03:28:05-07:00","id":1465618,"title":"","content":"Humanity for PCs is something we've been struggling with ever since we started playing in 1995, and I'm not sure we've reached a mutual understanding, as the game mechanics rarely explain the very essence of humanity for a vampire (or mortal for that matter). &quot;Evil deeds&quot; are not only often subjective - they also tend to change over time as society and morality does, and if you're an undead creature passing eons of time, you'll quickly get out of touch with what is &quot;good&quot; and what is &quot;evil&quot;. Hell, I'm 50 years old and I quite often have a rather hard time figuring out what is good and bad these days - can't imagine how off I would feel as a 200-year-old. <br /> <br /> Therefore, we made the decision to make Humanity a sort of anchor for the players ability to understand and interact with mortal society. To make it the filter through which they use their social skills when speaking to mortals, or even try to do business on a daily basis. We've made 7 the norm - lowering the diff. when above 7 and raising it when below (I believe it was thus i Revised).<br /> <br /> The conscience rolls are of course still debated vigorously in our group, as they still go by the whole &quot;good vs. evil&quot; aspect in the books, which doesn't really take old age and the lack of understanding your surroundings into account.<br /> <br /> So, to answer the initial question; my players are rarely bad in the sense of commiting evil acts ... they are more a challenge for me as an ST when having to explain to them why a 200 year old Nosferatu, who's been secluded from society for the most part of his unlife, has a hard time buying the right flowers at Leicester Square on a busy Friday night.<br /> <br /> V","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They do say, Mrs. M, that verbal insults hurt more than physical pain. They are of course wrong, as you will soon discover when I stick this toasting fork into your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> --E. Blackadder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24273-vincent","name":"Vincent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:28:36-07:00","id":1465638,"title":"","content":"It's interesting because I'm currently replaying OUT FOR BLOOD by Choice of Games and one of the funny things about the game is that the Kindred in the game (13th generation Toreador and Thin Bloods alike) are some of the nicer vampires you'd meet in the World of Darkness. Amanda goes out of her way to not kill people and the Thin Bloods only have one actual killer among them (maybe two).<br /> <br /> And the sheer HORROR AND DISGUST that our heroes display when they find out that A TEENAGER IS DEAD in the town is both believable as well as something that makes you think. Vampires get used to heavy body counts and accidents in a way that regular humans don't.<br /> <br /> In Out for Blood, you're out to destroy the guy who killed one person in the town and it drives the plot forward. Other Kindred? Whew. That's pretty effective as a sign they'd been careful up until now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:47:51-07:00","id":1465641,"title":"","content":"Vampires should go out of their way to not kill people. Investigations aren't worth the convenience of murdering your way through obstacles. Besides you've got plenty of money and spooky vampire powers so it's not really difficult to avoid murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-29-2021, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T09:21:51-07:00","id":1465664,"title":"","content":"What I have generally tried to keep in mind in my settings is that vampires are ultimately people first, albeit with the added burden of the beast pulling them towards destructive and addictive behaviors. I'd say the average Humanity level for most NPCs is around 5 (on the V20 scale). Decidedly more callous and jaded towards the suffering they inflict than most &quot;normal&quot; people (for a given value of normal), but not necessarily given to deliberate depravity unless in exceptional circumstances. For the older or more alien vampires I generally default to them hovering around Humanity 3. Still not cavalier about killing in cold blood unless provoked, but unfazed by most collateral damage they might leave in their wake.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat is always a bit tricky given the different takes on them over the years, but I tend to have the majority of rank and file Sabbat hanging out in that Humanity 3 zone. They won't go out of their way to commit atrocities unless they have a reason (siege, ritae, etc.) but they're pretty accustomed to casual evils. In my settings I like to have Paths be a bit special, with those that achieve them kind of becoming cult leaders and centers of gravity in their own right. In my version of the Sabbat feuds between incompatible Paths are a constantly simmering cold war within the Sword of Caine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 10-28-2021, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}